  "intro": "Before 1750 your address stood in grassy open forest of Spotted Gum and Broad-leaved Ironbark over a rich grassy, shrubby understorey, on the low foothills of the Lower Hunter. It is one of the most heavily cleared forests in the state — now a listed Endangered Ecological Community — so replanting it here genuinely matters. The plants below are indigenous to this exact community and grouped by the layer they fill. Plant the canopy first; the wildflowers, mat-rushes and grasses belong in the light beneath it.",
